    <!-- Safety / risk notices -->
    <string name="bt_info_title">Before you change anything</string>
    <string name="bt_info_body">These are system-level settings. What they actually do depends on your Android version and manufacturer, and some phones ignore or restore them. Changes stay until you undo them or reset.</string>
    <string name="bt_info_shizuku_active">Shizuku is connected — tweaks are applied the reliable way.</string>
    <string name="bt_info_shizuku_missing">Shizuku is not connected. Some tweaks may silently fail. Connecting Shizuku is strongly recommended.</string>
    <string name="bt_requires_android10">Power Save Mode tweaks need Android 10 or newer. Your device runs Android %1$s, where these settings use older names the system no longer accepts.</string>
    <string name="bt_doze_warning">Aggressive Doze can delay alarms, notifications, messages and background sync. If something stops arriving on time, set this back to System default.</string>

    <string name="risk_dialog_title">Understand the risks</string>
    <string name="risk_dialog_terminal">Commands run here execute with elevated system privileges, the same level as ADB. They can uninstall apps, delete data or leave your device unusable.

What you run is entirely your responsibility. The developer of this app cannot be held responsible for any damage, data loss or dangerous command you choose to execute.</string>
    <string name="risk_dialog_accept">I understand the risks</string>
    <string name="risk_dialog_decline">Cancel</string>
    <string name="terminal_disclaimer">Commands run with ADB-level privileges. You are responsible for what you run.</string>

    <string name="close_apps_info">Force-stopping apps can lose unsaved work and stop alarms, reminders and message delivery for those apps until you open them again. Add anything you rely on to the exclusion list below.</string>

